 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "7bK9gHcsBQAJ",
   "from": "Eric Enrique Flores De Gracia",
   "author": "b07b3e70f378f0b3",
   "date": "2024-12-30T22:18:59Z",
   "subject": "How to calculate the CI of P_a",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "I have run a point-distance sampling analyses with binned distances and could not find the way to calculate the confidence intervals for the probability detection function. I will appreciate any help.<div><br></div><div>Regards</div><div>Eric</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "0EDA4UNMBQAJ",
   "from": "Eric Rexstad",
   "author": "75e0b0abcbafbc7d",
   "date": "2024-12-31T08:01:41Z",
   "subject": "Re: [distance-sampling] How to calculate the CI of P_a",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nEric</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nWelcome to the list.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nThe summaries of fitted model objects produce only two measures of precision in estimates of detection probability: standard error and coefficient of variation. If you want a third measure of precision, namely confidence intervals, you&#39;ll need to calculate\r\n those yourself.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nHere is a bit of code that performs the confidence interval computation based upon the assumption the confidence interval is approximately log-normally distributed (Sect 6.2.1 of Buckland et al (2015):</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<img style=\"max-width:740px\" size=\"65122\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/54c43e1c040d0/image.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\"></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nlibrary(Distance)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\ndata(&quot;wren_snapshot&quot;)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\ncu &lt;- convert_units(&quot;meter&quot;, NULL, &quot;hectare&quot;)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\neasy &lt;- ds(wren_snapshot, key=&quot;hr&quot;, transect = &quot;point&quot;, convert_units = cu)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nout &lt;- summary(easy$ddf)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n# extract P_a and se from summary object</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nP_a &lt;- out$average.p</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nP_a_se &lt;- out$<a href=\"http://average.p.se\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://average.p.se&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471608342000&amp;usg=AOvVaw14kPXWPZhn7xUuQ04K9ftS\">average.p.se</a>[1,1]</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nP_a_cv &lt;- P_a_se / P_a</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n# assume degrees of freedom &gt;30</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nzed &lt;- 1.96</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n# use log-normal based confidence intervals</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nC &lt;- exp(zed*sqrt(log(1+P_a_cv^2)))</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nucb.log &lt;- P_a * C</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nlcb.log &lt;- P_a / C</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nprint(paste(&quot;CI bounds for P_a&quot;, round(lcb.log,4), round(ucb.log,4)))</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nIf you have questions, let me know.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"font-size:11pt\" color=\"#000000\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Eric Enrique Flores De Gracia &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sai...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 30 December 2024 18:43<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> distance-sampling &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [distance-sampling] How to calculate the CI of P_a</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I have run a point-distance sampling analyses with binned distances and could not find the way to calculate the confidence intervals for the probability detection function. I will appreciate any help.\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Regards</div>\r\n<div>Eric</div>\r\n<p></p></div></div>"
    ],
