     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">El martes, 31 de diciembre de 2024 a las 3:01:41 UTC-5, Eric Rexstad escribió:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nEric</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nWelcome to the list.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nThe summaries of fitted model objects produce only two measures of precision in estimates of detection probability: standard error and coefficient of variation. If you want a third measure of precision, namely confidence intervals, you&#39;ll need to calculate\r\n those yourself.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nHere is a bit of code that performs the confidence interval computation based upon the assumption the confidence interval is approximately log-normally distributed (Sect 6.2.1 of Buckland et al (2015):</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<img style=\"max-width:740px\" size=\"65122\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/54c43e1c040d0/image.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\"></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nlibrary(Distance)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\ndata(&quot;wren_snapshot&quot;)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\ncu &lt;- convert_units(&quot;meter&quot;, NULL, &quot;hectare&quot;)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\neasy &lt;- ds(wren_snapshot, key=&quot;hr&quot;, transect = &quot;point&quot;, convert_units = cu)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nout &lt;- summary(easy$ddf)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n# extract P_a and se from summary object</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nP_a &lt;- out$average.p</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nP_a_se &lt;- out$<a href=\"http://average.p.se\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://average.p.se&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471608345000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2myBTRCfTXMwfqvrcUJWQX\">average.p.se</a>[1,1]</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nP_a_cv &lt;- P_a_se / P_a</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n# assume degrees of freedom &gt;30</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nzed &lt;- 1.96</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n# use log-normal based confidence intervals</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nC &lt;- exp(zed*sqrt(log(1+P_a_cv^2)))</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nucb.log &lt;- P_a * C</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nlcb.log &lt;- P_a / C</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nprint(paste(&quot;CI bounds for P_a&quot;, round(lcb.log,4), round(ucb.log,4)))</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nIf you have questions, let me know.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"font-size:11pt\" color=\"#000000\"><b>From:</b> <a rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Eric Enrique Flores De Gracia &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">sai...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 30 December 2024 18:43<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> distance-sampling &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [distance-sampling] How to calculate the CI of P_a</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I have run a point-distance sampling analyses with binned distances and could not find the way to calculate the confidence intervals for the probability detection function. I will appreciate any help.\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Regards</div>\r\n<div>Eric</div>\r\n<p></p></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;distance-sampling&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a rel=\"nofollow\">distance-sampl...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/141e9d68-eed9-45d4-b13b-f052d924bae7n%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/141e9d68-eed9-45d4-b13b-f052d924bae7n%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471608346000&amp;usg=AOvVaw14rNOf5l1R_YKJHxW2AGbp\">\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/141e9d68-eed9-45d4-b13b-f052d924bae7n%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</blockquote></div>"
